Participate in care
CFR(s): 484.50(c)(4)(i,ii,iii,iv,v,vi,vii,viii)
Participate in, be informed about, and consent or refuse care in advance of and during treatment, where appropriate, with respect to--

(i) Completion of all assessments;

(ii) The care to be furnished, based on the comprehensive assessment;

(iii) Establishing and revising the plan of care;

(iv) The disciplines that will furnish the care;

(v) The frequency of visits;

(vi) Expected outcomes of care, including patient-identified goals, and anticipated risks and benefits;

(vii) Any factors that could impact treatment effectiveness; and

(viii) Any changes in the care to be furnished.

This Element is not met as evidenced by:
Based on staff interview, review of three (3) of three (3) medical records (#1, #2, #3), and review of facility documents, it was determined the facility failed to ensure that patients participate in establishing their plan of care. 

Reference: Facility policy titled, Plan of Care (POC)/Care Planning Process states, “… The patient has the right to Participate in… establishing and revising the plan of care… .”

1. Upon review of Medical Record #1, Medical Record #2, and Medical Record #3 the following was indicated:

a. There was no evidence that the Plan of Care was discussed with Patient #1, Patient #2, or Patient #3. 

 

2. The above findings were confirmed with Staff #1 on 9/14/21 at 2:00 PM.

