This Element is not met as evidenced by:
Based on medical record review of current patients, staff interview, and review of other facility documentation, it was determined that the facility failed to ensure that a "Risk for Infection" care plan is developed for each patient to ensure the consistent screening method for COVID-19 in one (1) out of six (6) medical records (#8).

Findings include:

1. An interview with Staff #1, an administrator, on 10/7/2021 at 10:56 AM, identified the process of creating a "Risk for Infection" care plan to assess all patients for COVID-19. 

2. A facility document was provided by Staff #1 that detailed an attendance sheet for a staff meeting dated 9/29/2021, that discussed the introduction of the "Risk for Infection" care plan for a new Start of Care (SoC).

3. A review of the medical record of Patient #8, revealed a SoC date of 10/04/2021. This medical record did not contain a "Risk of Infection" care plan. 

4. The above findings were confirmed with Staff #1 at the time of discovery.
